ernance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10). Recent headlines include layoff or workforce-reduction announcements.","financial_summary":["LiveWire Group, Inc. is a micro-cap consumer cyclical business with a $113M market cap on $26M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -18% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -227% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $57M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -14.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -296.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 1.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 19% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 94% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-3.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 302% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 80/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 122% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reviewing Lucid Group (NASDAQ:LCID) & LiveWire Group (NYSE:LVWR)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/reviewing-lucid-group-nasdaqlcid-livewire-group-nyselvwr.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793814291.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"LiveWire Group (LVWR) Stock Sinks As Q3 Earnings Deepen Restructuring Fears","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nyse-lvwr/livewire-group/news/livewire-group-lvwr-stock-sinks-as-q3-earnings-deepen-restru","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793410459.668,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.228,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","layoffs"]},{"title":"LiveWire Group (NYSE:LVWR) Stock Price Breaks Below 200-Day Moving Average \u2013 Here\u2019s What Happened","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/30/livew